From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Konstantin=20Sch=C3=B6ning?= <konstantin@lukianov.pp.ua>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 23:55:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] driver/at: stop closing logical channels this process does
 not own

logic_channel_open began by sending AT+CCHC for channels 1 through 4 on
every call. The early return above it proves this process holds none of
them, so each of those closes can only land on a channel belonging to
something else talking to the same card - a bearer's own stack, a modem
manager, another LPA - and it happens unprompted, on a card the driver has
just been pointed at and knows nothing about.

Make the sweep opt-in through LPAC_APDU_AT_RESET_CHANNELS. It is still the
way to recover a channel leaked by an earlier run; it is no longer the
default behaviour of opening one.

Found while reviewing the driver for use on a router where the modem
carrying the eUICC may also be carrying the uplink. No upstream pull
request covers this.
---
 driver/apdu/at.c        | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 driver/apdu/at_common.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/driver/apdu/at.c b/driver/apdu/at.c
index c6da1c8..5dfa43d 100644
--- a/driver/apdu/at.c
+++ b/driver/apdu/at.c
@@ -184,9 +184,21 @@ static int apdu_interface_logic_channel_open(struct euicc_ctx *ctx, const uint8_
         return logic_channel;
     }
 
-    for (int i = 1; i <= 4; i++) {
-        fprintf(fuart, "AT+CCHC=%d\r\n", i);
-        at_expect(NULL, NULL);
+    // Do not close logical channels 1-4 on every open. This process holds none
+    // of them - the early return above proves it - so each AT+CCHC here can
+    // only tear down a channel belonging to whatever else is talking to the
+    // card: a bearer's own stack, a modem manager, another LPA. That is a
+    // destructive act performed unprompted, on a card we have just been pointed
+    // at and know nothing about.
+    //
+    // The sweep is still the way to recover a channel leaked by an earlier run,
+    // so it stays - but as something a caller asks for, having decided that it
+    // owns the card.
+    if (getenv_or_default(ENV_AT_RESET_CHANNELS, false)) {
+        for (int i = 1; i <= 4; i++) {
+            fprintf(fuart, "AT+CCHC=%d\r\n", i);
+            at_expect(NULL, NULL);
+        }
     }
     fprintf(fuart, "AT+CCHO=\"");
     for (int i = 0; i < aid_len; i++) {
diff --git a/driver/apdu/at_common.h b/driver/apdu/at_common.h
index 43afde1..cb3c3f8 100644
--- a/driver/apdu/at_common.h
+++ b/driver/apdu/at_common.h
@@ -7,5 +7,6 @@
 
 #define ENV_AT_DEBUG APDU_ENV_NAME(AT, DEBUG)
 #define ENV_AT_DEVICE APDU_ENV_NAME(AT, DEVICE)
+#define ENV_AT_RESET_CHANNELS APDU_ENV_NAME(AT, RESET_CHANNELS)
 
 bool jprint_enumerate_devices(cJSON *data);
